.TH TNT-MODULES 7 "2026-09-18" "tnt-modules 0.3.1"
.SH NAME
tnt\-modules \- bundled chat commands for TNT
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
\fBTNT_MODULE_PATHS=\fP\fImodule-dir\fP\
[\fB:\fP\fImodule-dir\fP]...\ \fBtnt\fP
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tnt\-modules
supplies five chat-command modules and one optional policy module for
.BR tnt (8).
TNT starts each enabled module as a separate child process.
The bundled modules receive public chat messages.
A matching module may publish a public reply under its module name.
Several modules can be enabled together.
Other commands and normal conversation produce no bundled reply.
.SS Bundled commands
Command names are case-sensitive.
Each command must begin the message.
It must end the message or be followed by an ASCII space.
.TP
.BI "/roll [" count "]d" sides "[+/\-" modifier "]"
Roll dice and publish the individual rolls and total.
With no dice expression, roll one six-sided die.
The letter
.B d
is case-insensitive.
.I count
must be 1\(en20,
.I sides
must be 2\(en1000, and the absolute value of
.I modifier
must not exceed 10000.
An invalid expression produces a short usage reply.
.TP
.B /flip
Publish either heads or tails.
Trailing text is ignored.
.TP
.BI "/8ball [" question "]"
Publish one of the 20 classic Magic 8-Ball answers.
The question is optional.
.TP
.BI "/choose " option " | " option " [| " option ]...
Publish one randomly selected pipe-separated option.
Leading and trailing spaces and tabs are removed from each option.
At least two nonempty options are required;
otherwise the module produces a short usage reply.
.TP
.B /quote
Publish a random proverb from the module's built-in list.
Trailing text is ignored.
.SH SECURITY
.SS Optional guard module
.B guard-module
uses TNT's owner-granted
.B moderation:write
interface to inspect SSH session behavior and public message attempts.
It requires Python 3 with its standard library and a TNT build that supports
this permission.
It does not compare nicknames, require registration, or match prohibited
words.
Private sends share the source budget through metadata only; their bodies
are not passed to this module.
.PP
By default, the guard allows a burst of eight sends, refills two tokens per
second, and permits thirty sends per rolling minute.
The fifth consecutive copy of one public message within ten seconds is
rejected.
Blank public messages, including Unicode whitespace-only messages, are
rejected.
Five rejections within sixty seconds request a fifteen-minute source ban.
.PP
Three short sessions within twenty-four hours request a twenty-four-hour
ban when each session attempts a blank public message, sends no accepted
message, and leaves within three seconds.
Quiet readers who send no message do not count as probes.
The guard requests a three-second delay before public session notices;
an accepted message may announce the session sooner.
An empty session that leaves before the notice adds no public history.
.PP
Only source IPs are counted, with at most 512 source ledgers by default.
Message and duplicate counters are held in memory.
Recent probe times are saved privately in
.I TNT_STATE_DIR/guard-probes.json
with mode 0600 and survive a module restart.
The file contains no message bodies.
Source bans are applied, stored, and removed by TNT's owner-control API.
These rules do not establish who operates a source or what its intent is.
.PP
Enable the guard alongside any chat-command modules:
.EX
TNT_MODULE_GRANTS=guard-module
TNT_MODULE_PATHS=/usr/local/libexec/tnt/modules/guard-module
export TNT_MODULE_GRANTS TNT_MODULE_PATHS
tnt
.EE
.PP
Append to existing grants and module paths when enabling it on a configured
server.
Use TNT's local
.B --list-bans
and
.B --unban
options to review and remove restrictions.
An IP may be shared by a network or anonymity relay.
.PP
If the guard stalls or returns an invalid response, TNT disables it and
records the failure in its journal and private audit.
Basic chat remains available; persisted bans remain enforced.
Restart TNT after fixing the policy or its configuration.
The guard currently covers TNT's SSH paths; WebSocket account policy and
cross-proxy source attribution require separate integration.
.SS Configuration
.B TNT_GUARD_CONFIG
may name an operator-owned JSON file overriding integer settings:
.BR burst ,
.BR per_second ,
.BR per_minute ,
.BR duplicate_limit ,
.BR duplicate_window ,
.BR violation_limit ,
.BR violation_window ,
.BR ban_seconds ,
.BR probe_limit ,
.BR probe_window ,
.BR probe_ban_seconds ,
.BR notice_delay_ms ,
and
.BR max_sources .
Time windows and ban durations use seconds; the notice delay uses
milliseconds.
Values must be positive and at most 86400, with at most 4096 sources and a
notice delay of at most 30000 milliseconds.
Unknown settings cause startup to fail visibly.
.SS Process privileges
Module processes run as the TNT service account.
They inherit its user, group, filesystem, and network privileges.
They are not an operating-system sandbox.
Manifest permissions describe protocol capabilities;
they do not restrict system calls or resource access.
.PP
The bundled modules perform no network operations.
Review any replacement or additional module before enabling it,
keep its directory from being writable by untrusted users,
and run TNT under a dedicated least-privileged account.
Use an operating-system sandbox or container for stronger isolation.
.PP
TNT can disable a module that stalls or violates the protocol.
That supervision does not contain filesystem or network side effects.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TNT_MODULE_PATHS
A colon-separated list of module directories read when TNT starts.
Each directory must contain
.I tnt\-module.json
and the executable entrypoint named by that manifest.
An empty or unset value disables external modules.
TNT enables at most eight valid modules.
Restart TNT after changing the value.
.IP
Relative directories are resolved from TNT's working directory.
Use absolute directories in service configuration.
For the default
.B make install
layout,
enable the dice and coin modules with:
.EX
TNT_MODULE_PATHS=/usr/local/libexec/tnt/modules/roll\-module:\e
/usr/local/libexec/tnt/modules/flip\-module \e
    tnt
.EE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/local/libexec/tnt/modules/
Default installation root for the six module directories.
Changing
.B PREFIX
or
.B MODULEDIR
when running
.B make install
changes this path.
.TP
.I modules/
Contains the bundled
.BR 8ball\-module ,
.BR choose\-module ,
.BR flip\-module ,
.BR quote\-module ,
and
.B roll\-module
directories in the source distribution.
Pass an individual child directory, not this parent directory, in
.BR TNT_MODULE_PATHS .
Each child contains its manifest, executable entrypoint, JSON parser, and
module program.
.SH VERSIONS
The bundled manifests require TNT 1.1.0 or later and use the
.B tnt.module.v1
protocol.
TNT checks the manifest protocol and startup handshake.
It enables only modules that pass both checks.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tntctl (1),
.BR tnt\-module\-protocol (7),
.BR tnt (8)
